---
/**
 * The moving ground behind the plans.
 *
 * `public/videos/Blue_3D_Hero.mp4`, sitting behind whatever it is dropped into
 * — the heading and the grid together on /pricing/ and /social-media/, the band
 * on the home page. Two places render it, which is why it is a component: the
 * markup and the rules below have to stay identical in both or the two surfaces
 * drift apart.
 *
 * It replaces a still that was a CSS `background` with `100% 100%`, which
 * stretched the picture to the box and distorted it — hexagons drawn round came
 * out as ovals. A video cannot be a CSS background at all, so this is a real
 * element, and `object-fit: cover` is what a background image would have called
 * `cover`: fill the box, keep the aspect, crop the overflow. Nothing here
 * stretches at any viewport.
 *
 * The parent must be a positioned, isolated stacking context — both callers are.
 */
---

<video
	class="plans-field"
	src="/videos/Blue_3D_Hero.mp4"
	autoplay
	muted
	loop
	playsinline
	preload="metadata"
	aria-hidden="true"
	tabindex="-1"
	disablepictureinpicture
	disableRemotePlayback></video>

{/*
	The scrim, over the footage.

	A separate element rather than a pseudo-element on the video, because a
	<video> is a replaced element and does not render ::before or ::after. Both
	sit at `z-index: -1`; this one comes second in the DOM, which is what puts it
	on top of the footage and still under everything the band renders.
*/}
<div class="plans-field__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
	/*
		Behind the content, out of the flow, and untouchable. `z-index: -1` puts it
		under everything the band renders without needing a z-index on any of it —
		the parent's `isolation: isolate` is what keeps that negative index from
		escaping the section.
	*/
	.plans-field {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		z-index: -1;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		pointer-events: none;
	}

	/*
		Deliberately light. The footage is the point; this only has to take the top
		off it so white type has something to sit on and the cards stay the
		brightest thing in the band.

		Weighted to the top, where the heading and lede are, easing to a flat wash
		by the time it reaches the grid — the cards paint their own near-opaque ink
		and do not need help.
	*/
	.plans-field__scrim {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		z-index: -1;
		pointer-events: none;
		background: linear-gradient(
			180deg,
			rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55) 0%,
			rgb(0 0 0 / 0.38) 26%,
			rgb(0 0 0 / 0.28) 55%,
			rgb(0 0 0 / 0.34) 100%
		);
	}

	/*
		A moving ground behind a price list is decoration, and decoration is the
		first thing to drop for someone who has asked for less motion. The band
		keeps its own dark ground underneath, so removing this leaves a flat
		section rather than a hole — and the scrim goes with it, since there is
		nothing left to take the top off.
	*/
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.plans-field,
		.plans-field__scrim {
			display: none;
		}
	}
</style>
